  {
   "_id": 11421,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2008\" data-start=\"1821\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"2008\" data-start=\"1821\">Symbolic programming automates calculus operations without manual steps. Using Sympy:</p>\n\n<p>from sympy import symbols, diff, integrate, limit</p>\n\n<p>x = symbols(&#39;x&#39;)<br />\nf = x**3</p>\n\n<p>d = diff(f, x)<br />\ni = integrate(f, x)<br />\nl = limit(1/x, x, float(&#39;inf&#39;))</p>\n\n<p>print(d) &nbsp;# 3*x**2<br />\nprint(i) &nbsp;# x**4/4<br />\nprint(l) &nbsp;# 0<br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"4596\" data-start=\"4470\">This analysis shows how symbolic tools can solve problems exactly, unlike numerical methods which may involve rounding errors.</p>\n",
